      "id": 478672,
      "username": "ablishek",
      "name": "Abhishek Shah",
      "created_at": "2025-08-22T22:33:06.454Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/syed_anas\">@Syed_Anas</a>,</p>\n<p>Thanks for writing, followed the steps but back to zero. Here is what I did:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Create Item Alternatives.<br>\n<div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/0/2/02798eac3121a75825f3cac13ae16b073b16ffc6.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/02798eac3121a75825f3cac13ae16b073b16ffc6\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/0/2/02798eac3121a75825f3cac13ae16b073b16ffc6_2_690x215.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"lTocgktytseq2C3THk1JOdiaR8\" width=\"690\" height=\"215\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/0/2/02798eac3121a75825f3cac13ae16b073b16ffc6_2_690x215.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/0/2/02798eac3121a75825f3cac13ae16b073b16ffc6_2_1035x322.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/0/2/02798eac3121a75825f3cac13ae16b073b16ffc6.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"242424\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1202×375 30.3 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></li>\n<li>Went into Material Request, clicked on the Create → Material Issue</li>\n<li>This created a Stock Entry. Then inside stock entry as I updated an item to its substitute upon saving it threw an error that item was not in material request. Also based on the documentation you provided I saw that other doctypes had a designated Allow Alternative button or checkbox. But Stock Entry doesn’t have them. Is this a design oversight or am I missing something?</li>\n</ol>",
